Subject: [PATCH] pandora: put the GPU table pool back to 4 MiB and 4 clients

Every kernel that renders a black screen was built after 0332, and every kernel that reaches
the lock screen was built before it: loader-gpu15.img (log29/30/31/38/41, lock screen, 10-41
frames, 314-337 IOAcceleratorES queries from backboardd) has no "client windows taken" and no
"table pages" string in its text segment, while k341/k343/k346/k348 all do.  Same pack, same
boot-args, same config table (byte-identical gIOKernelConfigTables), so the personality, the
IOAcceleratorES class and the es_* threads that were blamed in 0337 cannot be it: 0337 removed
the personality and log43 still froze.

What 0332 changes for a boot that is already at pandora_gpu=15 is the shape of the GPU's
memory: GPU_TABLE_PAGES 1024 -> 2048 makes the level-9 table pool a single 8 MiB
kmem_alloc_contig(KMA_PERMANENT) instead of 4 MiB, and GPU_MAX_CLIENTS 4 -> 15 grows
gpu_clients[] and the gpu_watch() frame (last[clients][160] = 2400 bytes on that thread's
stack).  log43/37/39/40 all stop the same way: backboardd opens SweetHIDTouch and
SweetHIDButtons at 14.15 s and then issues no further IOKit call for 32 s, never asks for
IOMobileFramebuffer, and the display is never brought up.

Go back to 4 MiB and 4 clients to confirm that split before redesigning the pool: this is a
bisect step, not the final shape.  A wider pool has to be introduced so that nothing a boot
needs moves or grows.

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_gpu.c b/bsd/dev/pandora_gpu.c
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_gpu.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_gpu.c
@@ -544,7 +544,7 @@ gpu_level3(void)
 #define GMU_ASID          1u
 #define GMU_SLOT          2u
 #define GMU_TABLE_PAGES   64u
-#define GPU_TABLE_PAGES   2048u     /* 8 MiB: the level-9 tables plus room for ~4 GiB of later 4K maps (0332: more clients) */
+#define GPU_TABLE_PAGES   1024u     /* 4 MiB: the level-9 tables plus room for ~2 GiB of later 4K maps */
 #define GPU_INPUT_BITS    36u       /* 0219: the GPU context's addresses; room for the clients' 4 GiB windows */
 
 struct gmu_buf {
@@ -2297,7 +2297,7 @@ LCK_GRP_DECLARE(gpu_lck_grp, "pandora_gpu");
 LCK_MTX_DECLARE(gpu_lock, &gpu_lck_grp);
 
 #define GPU_MAX_BOS       4096u
-#define GPU_MAX_CLIENTS   15u       /* 0332: the 4 GiB windows at 4..64 GiB of the 36-bit space (4 with the 32-bit layout) */
+#define GPU_MAX_CLIENTS   4u
 #define GPU_MAX_IBS       128u      /* NativeAdrenoAbiMaxBuffers (tools/turnip/abi_128.py, 0194) */
 struct gpu_bo {
 	bool used;
